From 3db279110375b75d19e17dddd38fb3a4860b9dcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:47:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 13/40] Metal diamond engine: runs for the excitation and the
 dispersive materials (snapshot cg25)

The per-tile lists of the excitation entries and of the dispersive elements (conducting
sheets, Drude/Lorentz, Debye) become runs: the entries of one field value, or the elements
of one extension at one cell, in the CPU's order, with the float index precomputed. One
thread applies a run in that order, so every value gets the CPU's arithmetic in the CPU's
sequence, and:
- the excitation is applied in parallel instead of by one thread per tile; tiles without
  entries for the step type skip the stage and its barrier; without a signal period the
  signal index skips the modulo (0 <= pos <= ts, so pos % (ts+1) was pos);
- the orders of a dispersive extension share one Pre pass and one Apply pass (the two
  orders of a conducting sheet had a pass and a barrier each), steps without ADE work (the
  sheets' H steps) skip those stages and barriers, and an Apply barrier only follows work;
  a position repeated within an order no longer needs the serial path;
- the per-tile run offsets are read once per dispatch instead of once per step.
Grids need fewer than 65536 lines in x and y (x and y share a word in a run); larger ones
run the CPU loops.

Paired interleaved A/B against cg24 (emsKit bench/abtest.py, 5 rounds, other processes on
4-5 cores): GCPW line x1.24 [1.20-1.29], SMA launch x1.15 [1.14-1.21], notch x3 and patch
x5 x1.00, notch tutorial x0.96 [0.93-1.01] (the next commit gets it back), the patch
tutorial within the noise at that load. Step by step at 1-4 other cores: the sheet runs
x1.20 on the GCPW line, the excitation runs x1.16 on the SMA launch (3851 entries), the
offsets read once x1.014 more on the GCPW line.

emsKit diamond_check.sh 54 of 54. All six benchmark models bit-identical to the
multithreaded engine with OPENEMS_FTZ=1 (probes rel 0, S-parameters 0 dB). The CPU engines
are unchanged.

